{"call_id": "545ace18272f449d8973dc50662b8d0f", "success": true, "result_file": "/data/nly/Agent-Aware-Trajectory-Level-Query/benchmark/fullbench/runs/fad/GITHUB_REPOS/query1/full-01/results/545ace18272f449d8973dc50662b8d0f.json", "row_count": null, "preview": "{\"submitted\": true, \"answer\": \"Among repositories that do not use Python, approximately 13.8% of their README.md files include copyright information.\\n\\nMethodology:\\n- The artifacts database contains 204 README.md files (case-insensitive match on paths ending in \\\"readme.md\\\", at root or nested) across 200 repositories with retrievable content.\\n- These repos were matched against the metadata database's languages table (178 of 200 found). A repo \\\"uses Python\\\" if its language_description mentions \\\"Python\\\"; otherwise it is classified as non-Python.\\n- A README.md is considered to include copyright information if its content contains the word \\\"copyright\\\" (case-insensitive) or the © symbol.\\n\\nResults:\\n- Non-Python repositories with README.md files: 135, containing 138 README.md files.\\n- README.md files containing copyright information: 19 of 138 → proportion = 19/138 ≈ 0.138 (13.8%).\\n- At the repository level: 19 of 135 non-Python repos (14.1%) have at least one README.md with copyright information.\\n- Sensitivity check: if the 22 repos absent from the metadata languages table are also counted as non-Python, the figure is 21/160 ≈ 13.1%.\\n\\nAnswer: about 13.8% (19 out of 138 README.md files from non-Python repositories).\\n\"}", "truncated": false}
